  "description": "With lambda_max, that many of the AWS half's ec2_max tiles are Lambda tiles (lam-<n>, tiles lambda:<k>) and the rest EC2 tiles. The half keeps its places and is one grid, its EC2 tiles first. A Lambda tile without an execution environment holds its place, dark, with its phase. A race relaunches every tile; the EC2 tiles and the Lambda tiles each get their own race number and scoreboard row. A Lambda tile's time ends when the coordinator sees its new environment's first frame, less a capacity wait Lambda named; its warm invoke time is kept beside it and never counted. A viewer's relaunch of a Lambda tile waits 90 s after its last launch, as an EC2 tile's does.",
